    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "rows = []\n",
    "for name in list_products():\n",
    "    s = get_spec(name)\n",
    "    n_files = len(sorted(s.directory.glob(s.glob))) if s.directory.exists() else 0\n",
    "    rows.append({\"product\": name, \"family\": s.family, \"res_m\": s.native_res_m,\n",
    "                 \"temporal\": s.temporal, \"monthly\": s.month_parser is not None,\n",
    "                 \"dir_exists\": s.directory.exists(), \"n_files\": n_files,\n",
    "                 \"directory\": str(s.directory)})\n",
    "pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index(\"product\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell05",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Load ONE product for ONE year, and inspect every sub-step\n",
    "\n",
    "We trace MCD64A1 / 2017. First the raw clip (note it keeps a singleton `band` dim), then the\n",
    "standardized annual mask the toolkit actually uses (band squeezed, months OR'd)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell06",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "product, year = \"MCD64A1\", 2017\n",
    "spec = get_spec(product)\n",
    "\n",
    "# (a) the monthly files the loader will group for this year\n",
    "files = sorted(spec.directory.glob(spec.glob))\n",
    "files_2017 = [f for f in files if spec.year_parser(f) == year]\n",
    "print(f\"{product}: {len(files_2017)} monthly files for {year}\")\n",
    "for f in files_2017[:3]:\n",
    "    print(\"   \", f.name, \"-> month\", spec.month_parser(f))\n",
    "\n",
    "# (b) raw clip of a single month (in memory). Still has a band dimension.\n",
    "one = clip_raster_to_mask(files_2017[0], aoi)\n",
    "print(\"\\nsingle clipped month -> dims:\", dict(one.sizes), \"| CRS:\", one.rio.crs)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell07",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# (c) the standardized ANNUAL mask (band squeezed, 12 months OR'd, True=burned)\n",
    "mask = load_standardized(product, year, aoi)\n",
    "print(\"annual mask name :\", mask.name)\n",
    "print(\"dims             :\", dict(mask.sizes))\n",
    "print(\"CRS              :\", mask.rio.crs, \"(native sinusoidal)\")\n",
    "print(\"burned pixels    :\", int((mask.values == True).sum()))\n",
    "mask.astype(\"uint8\").plot(); plt.title(f\"{product} {year} annual burned mask (native grid)\"); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell08",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. The common grid (the resolution-confound fix)\n",
    "\n",
    "`build_common_grid` makes an empty EPSG:5070 reference grid over the AOI; `to_common_grid` warps any\n",
    "product onto it with `how=\"max\"`. Every product is matched to THIS grid, so none is privileged."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell09",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "grid = build_common_grid(aoi, res_m=500.0)\n",
    "print(\"common grid CRS  :\", grid.rio.crs)\n",
    "print(\"common grid shape:\", dict(grid.sizes))\n",
    "print(\"pixel size (m)   :\", grid.rio.resolution())\n",
    "\n",
    "mask_cg = to_common_grid(mask.astype(\"float32\"), grid, how=\"max\") > 0\n",
    "print(\"\\nmask on common grid -> dims:\", dict(mask_cg.sizes), \"| CRS:\", mask_cg.rio.crs)\n",
    "mask_cg.astype(\"uint8\").plot(); plt.title(f\"{product} {year} on 500 m EPSG:5070 common grid\"); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell10",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Annual burned-area series — native vs common-grid (Humber Figure 3)\n",
    "\n",
    "`mode=\"native\"` uses each product's own pixel area; `mode=\"common_grid\"` puts everyone on the shared\n",
    "500 m grid first. Comparing the two shows how much of any product difference is just resolution."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell11",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "products_ba = [\"MCD64A1\", \"GABAM\", \"FireCCI51\", \"USGS_BA\"]   # absent ones skip with a warning\n",
    "years = range(2001, 2022)\n",
    "\n",
    "area_native = annual_burned_area_series(products_ba, years, aoi, mode=\"native\")\n",
    "area_cg     = annual_burned_area_series(products_ba, years, aoi, mode=\"common_grid\")\n",
    "display(area_native.head())\n",
    "display(area_cg.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell12",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_annual_series(area_native, title=\"NC burned area — native resolution\"); plt.show()\n",
    "plot_annual_series(area_cg,     title=\"NC burned area — 500 m common grid\"); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Agreement matrices (\"confusion-matrix\" heatmaps)\n",
    "\n",
    "VIIRS is included as the independent occurrence check. Binary spatial agreement (Jaccard, kappa) and\n",
    "temporal correlation of annual totals answer different questions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell14",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "products_all = [\"MCD64A1\", \"GABAM\", \"FireCCI51\", \"USGS_BA\", \"VIIRS\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "jac = agreement_matrix(products_all, years, aoi, method=\"jaccard\", pooling=\"cells\")\n",
    "kap = agreement_matrix(products_all, years, aoi, method=\"kappa\",   pooling=\"cells\")\n",
    "cor = agreement_matrix(products_ba,  years, aoi, method=\"pearson\", pooling=\"years\")\n",
    "display(jac.round(2)); display(cor.round(2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell15",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_agreement_heatmap(jac, title=\"Spatial agreement (Jaccard)\", vmin=0, vmax=1); plt.show()\n",
    "plot_agreement_heatmap(cor, title=\"Annual-total correlation (Pearson)\", vmin=-1, vmax=1); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "300868d8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5b. Pairwise scatterplots — total least squares (Humber-style)\n",
    "\n",
    "Humber compares two products at a time with **total least squares** (orthogonal regression, which\n",
    "minimises perpendicular distance — right when *both* axes have error) and reports **RMSE** against the\n",
    "**y = x** line. Each scatter point is one common-grid cell (our per-spatial-unit analogue of their per-TSA\n",
    "points), holding that cell's burned fraction.\n",
    "\n",
    "`tls_slope` near 1 = the two products agree on magnitude; the `tls_slope` matrix is **asymmetric**\n",
    "(entry [a, b] uses a as x, b as y). RMSE is symmetric. (TLS slope / RMSE on *totals* stay on the\n",
    "burned-area products, which share km² units.)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5adbb563",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# scatter of two products' per-cell burned fraction in one year, with TLS + y=x\n",
    "x, y = product_pair_scatter(\"MCD64A1\", \"GABAM\", 2017, aoi)\n",
    "print(\"n scatter points (cells):\", x.size)\n",
    "if x.size:\n",
    "    print(\"TLS slope, intercept:\", total_least_squares(x, y), \"| RMSE:\", round(rmse(x, y), 4))\n",
    "    plot_product_scatter(\n",
    "        x, y,\n",
    "        xlabel=\"MCD64A1 burned fraction / cell\",\n",
    "        ylabel=\"GABAM burned fraction / cell\",\n",
    "        title=\"MCD64A1 vs GABAM, 2017 (per 500 m cell)\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# TLS-slope and RMSE matrices on per-period totals (burned-area products, km^2)\n",
    "tls = agreement_matrix(products_ba, years, aoi, method=\"tls_slope\", pooling=\"years\")\n",
    "err = agreement_matrix(products_ba, years, aoi, method=\"rmse\",      pooling=\"years\")\n",
    "display(tls.round(2)); display(err.round(1))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b61e3238",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Overlay map for a chosen year\n",
    "\n",
    "`stack_on_common_grid` aligns every product for the year; `plot_overlay_map` shows where a pair agree\n",
    "(1 = A only, 2 = B only, 3 = both)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell17",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "stack_2017 = stack_on_common_grid(products_ba, 2017, aoi, binary=True)\n",
    "print(\"products present in 2017 stack:\", list(stack_2017))\n",
    "if {\"GABAM\", \"MCD64A1\"} <= set(stack_2017):\n",
    "    plot_overlay_map(stack_2017, aoi, 2017, pair=(\"GABAM\", \"MCD64A1\")); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell18",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Monthly mode\n",
    "\n",
    "One flag: `temporal_unit=\"month\"`. Annual-only products (GABAM, USGS_BA, ...) are dropped; the monthly\n",
    "products + VIIRS remain. The series index becomes month-start Timestamps."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell19",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "area_monthly = annual_burned_area_series(\n",
    "    [\"MCD64A1\", \"FireCCI51\", \"FireCCIS311\"], range(2017, 2019),\n",
    "    aoi, mode=\"common_grid\", temporal_unit=\"month\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "display(area_monthly.head(14))\n",
    "plot_annual_series(area_monthly, title=\"Monthly burned area (2017-2018)\"); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4b753e9d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7b. Temporal heat map (Humber-style)\n",
    "\n",
    "`period_totals_series` gives, per month, burned-area km² for each product and the VIIRS active-fire\n",
    "**detection count**. `plot_temporal_heatmap` lays this out as products × time, with VIIRS as the bottom\n",
    "reference row. By default each row is normalised to its own max so the *timing* is comparable across\n",
    "products despite the different units — bright cells lining up vertically mean a product's burn\n",
    "detections coincide with active fire."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e3234afb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "totals_m = period_totals_series(\n",
    "    [\"MCD64A1\", \"FireCCI51\", \"FireCCIS311\", \"VIIRS\"], range(2017, 2019),\n",
    "    aoi, temporal_unit=\"month\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "display(totals_m.head(14))\n",
    "plot_temporal_heatmap(\n",
    "    totals_m, normalize=\"row\",\n",
    "    title=\"Monthly burned area by product vs VIIRS active fire (2017-2018)\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
